  "section": "Movie Facts # 5 of 10",
  "description": "According to the actors who appeared in The Empire Strikes Back, director Irvin Kershner would encourage group discussions and improvisations. He would do many takes of each scene, in contrast to George Lucas, who would generally stick to the script and usually do about three takes. Although reviews in 1980 were mixed, the film has grown in stature over the years and is often cited as the favorite of Star Wars fans. It was selected in 2010 to be preserved by the Library of Congress as part of its National Film Registry."
